# Normalize line endings to LF for anything git detects as text, regardless of which OS or tool
# commits it - without this, files land with whatever line ending the committing client happened
# to write, and every downstream sync (see .github/workflows/sync-and-publish.yml) that compares
# this repo's blobs against another copy sees a full-file rewrite for pure whitespace noise.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit safety net on top of git's content-sniffing heuristic for this repo's actual binary
# assets (branding art, jarred dependencies) - never want these run through a text filter.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.jar binary
